  "lectures": [
    {
      "id": "43341108",
      "title": "User Signup: Extracting & Validating User Input",
      "lectureOrder": 207,
      "videoOrder": 193,
      "sourceHash": "e218cc06a8d034f5ae92b094fd7c3c54b2269be847a69b78143b763498af6317",
      "cues": [
        {
          "id": 1,
          "start": 0.66,
          "end": 1.8,
          "en": "So let's get started",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 2,
          "start": 1.8,
          "end": 4.47,
          "en": "working on this website here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 3,
          "start": 4.47,
          "end": 8.22,
          "en": "And I wanna start with creating user accounts,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 4,
          "start": 8.22,
          "end": 11.73,
          "en": "because, of course, we need user accounts first",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 5,
          "start": 11.73,
          "end": 14.853,
          "en": "before we then can log users in.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 6,
          "start": 15.9,
          "end": 17.13,
          "en": "So, therefore, I wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 7,
          "start": 17.13,
          "end": 20.55,
          "en": "that if we click this Create Account button here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 8,
          "start": 20.55,
          "end": 23.16,
          "en": "we submit the entered data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 9,
          "start": 23.16,
          "end": 25.23,
          "en": "and I therefor wanna make sure",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 10,
          "start": 25.23,
          "end": 28.47,
          "en": "that only valid data is accepted,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 11,
          "start": 28.47,
          "end": 30.57,
          "en": "and we create a new user",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 12,
          "start": 30.57,
          "end": 33.033,
          "en": "with that email-password combination.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 13,
          "start": 34.02,
          "end": 36.93,
          "en": "Now, as I mentioned in the previous lecture already,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 14,
          "start": 36.93,
          "end": 38.61,
          "en": "this starting project",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 15,
          "start": 38.61,
          "end": 41.25,
          "en": "already comes with a database in the end",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 16,
          "start": 41.25,
          "end": 43.47,
          "en": "that will contain a user's table,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 17,
          "start": 43.47,
          "end": 47.88,
          "en": "where we need to store a unique email and a password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 18,
          "start": 47.88,
          "end": 51.87,
          "en": "So that's exactly what I wanna do as a first step now.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 19,
          "start": 51.87,
          "end": 54.54,
          "en": "And, therefore, on this auth form here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 20,
          "start": 54.54,
          "end": 57.3,
          "en": "I wanna add a Server Action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 21,
          "start": 57.3,
          "end": 59.43,
          "en": "that handles the form of submission,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 22,
          "start": 59.43,
          "end": 62.22,
          "en": "where we extract the email-password combination",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 23,
          "start": 62.22,
          "end": 64.143,
          "en": "and store it in the database.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 24,
          "start": 65.34,
          "end": 70.28999999999999,
          "en": "And I actually don't just wanna extract and store that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 25,
          "start": 70.28999999999999,
          "end": 74.55,
          "en": "Instead, I also wanna validate it so that we, for example,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 26,
          "start": 74.55,
          "end": 78.36,
          "en": "catch values that aren't valid email addresses,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 27,
          "start": 78.36,
          "end": 80.46000000000001,
          "en": "or potentially also passwords",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 28,
          "start": 80.46000000000001,
          "end": 82.68299999999999,
          "en": "which are too short, let's say.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 29,
          "start": 83.85,
          "end": 85.41,
          "en": "And therefore, as a first step,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 30,
          "start": 85.41,
          "end": 88.05,
          "en": "I'll add a new folder in this project,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 31,
          "start": 88.05,
          "end": 89.85,
          "en": "in the root project folder,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 32,
          "start": 89.85,
          "end": 91.32,
          "en": "and I'll name it actions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 33,
          "start": 91.32,
          "end": 94.35,
          "en": "because here, I wanna store my Server Actions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 34,
          "start": 94.35,
          "end": 96.33,
          "en": "in separate files.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 35,
          "start": 96.33,
          "end": 99.53999999999999,
          "en": "That's of course not something you have to do,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 36,
          "start": 99.53999999999999,
          "end": 100.89,
          "en": "as you learned in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 37,
          "start": 100.89,
          "end": 102.993,
          "en": "but it is something I will do here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 38,
          "start": 104.126,
          "end": 107.94,
          "en": "And therefore here I'll add an auth.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 39,
          "start": 107.94,
          "end": 112.17,
          "en": "or maybe auth-actions.js to make it clear",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 40,
          "start": 112.17,
          "end": 114.47999999999999,
          "en": "that we'll store some Server Actions in there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 41,
          "start": 114.47999999999999,
          "end": 116.163,
          "en": "The name of course is up to you.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 42,
          "start": 117.33,
          "end": 122.1,
          "en": "And then in that file, I'll add this 'use server' directive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 43,
          "start": 122.1,
          "end": 123.45,
          "en": "at the top of this file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 44,
          "start": 123.45,
          "end": 125.97,
          "en": "because as you learned in this course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 45,
          "start": 125.97,
          "end": 129.54,
          "en": "if you wanna create functions that should serve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 46,
          "start": 129.54,
          "end": 133.68,
          "en": "as Server Actions in a NextJS application,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 47,
          "start": 133.68,
          "end": 137.31,
          "en": "you need to add this 'use server' directive here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 48,
          "start": 137.31,
          "end": 141.06,
          "en": "at the top of the file where you create those functions",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 49,
          "start": 141.06,
          "end": 144.12,
          "en": "or inside of the functions themselves.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 50,
          "start": 144.12,
          "end": 147.363,
          "en": "And here, since I have a separate file, I add it at the top.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 51,
          "start": 148.32,
          "end": 150.66,
          "en": "Okay, so that's the first step.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 52,
          "start": 150.66,
          "end": 155.66,
          "en": "The next step is to create a new async function in here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 53,
          "start": 155.88,
          "end": 157.89,
          "en": "and it must be async as you learned.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 54,
          "start": 157.89,
          "end": 161.34,
          "en": "Server Actions are async functions,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 55,
          "start": 161.34,
          "end": 163.02,
          "en": "which I'll name, signup.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 56,
          "start": 163.02,
          "end": 164.61,
          "en": "The name of course is up to you,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 57,
          "start": 164.61,
          "end": 167.91,
          "en": "but this name should be pretty descriptive",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 58,
          "start": 167.91,
          "end": 171,
          "en": "regarding what this function will do.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 59,
          "start": 171,
          "end": 173.07,
          "en": "Well, and then this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 60,
          "start": 173.07,
          "end": 176.16,
          "en": "will eventually receive some form data as you learned",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 61,
          "start": 176.16,
          "end": 179.28,
          "en": "since I plan on using it as a Server Action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 62,
          "start": 179.28,
          "end": 182.55,
          "en": "and since I plan on assigning it to a form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 63,
          "start": 182.55,
          "end": 186.963,
          "en": "And then NextJS will automatically provide that form data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 64,
          "start": 188.34,
          "end": 192.12,
          "en": "And here, I'll then extract my email from that form data,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 65,
          "start": 192.12,
          "end": 194.94,
          "en": "with formData.get email,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 66,
          "start": 194.94,
          "end": 199.94,
          "en": "and my password with formData.get password, like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 67,
          "start": 201.15,
          "end": 204.24,
          "en": "And of course, these names, email, and password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 68,
          "start": 204.24,
          "end": 207.27,
          "en": "are not some random names I picked here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 69,
          "start": 207.27,
          "end": 209.94,
          "en": "but instead, these are the names you'll find",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 70,
          "start": 209.94,
          "end": 214.94,
          "en": "in the auth form here, assigned to the name attribute.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 71,
          "start": 216.87,
          "end": 219.03,
          "en": "So, that will allow us to retrieve",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 72,
          "start": 219.03,
          "end": 221.37,
          "en": "the email and the password.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 73,
          "start": 221.37,
          "end": 223.17000000000002,
          "en": "And with that retrieved,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 74,
          "start": 223.17000000000002,
          "end": 226.86,
          "en": "we of course eventually wanna store it in the database,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 75,
          "start": 226.86,
          "end": 229.38,
          "en": "so we want to create a new user.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 76,
          "start": 229.38,
          "end": 233.43,
          "en": "But first, I wanna validate that data.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 77,
          "start": 233.43,
          "end": 237.24,
          "en": "And there would be various ways of doing that.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 78,
          "start": 237.24,
          "end": 241.26,
          "en": "I'll validate that data by creating an errors object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 79,
          "start": 241.26,
          "end": 243.93,
          "en": "which initially is an empty object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 80,
          "start": 243.93,
          "end": 246.78,
          "en": "And I'll then check if my email",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 81,
          "start": 246.78,
          "end": 251.01,
          "en": "does not include an @ symbol.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 82,
          "start": 251.01,
          "end": 254.343,
          "en": "So a pretty basic check, but better than nothing.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 83,
          "start": 255.24,
          "end": 256.59,
          "en": "And if that's the case,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 84,
          "start": 256.59,
          "end": 260.22,
          "en": "I wanna add a new field to that errors object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 85,
          "start": 260.22,
          "end": 262.89,
          "en": "let's say, a field named, email,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 86,
          "start": 262.89,
          "end": 264.96,
          "en": "which contains the error message.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 87,
          "start": 264.96,
          "end": 266.377,
          "en": "And in my case here, that will be,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 88,
          "start": 266.377,
          "end": 269.4,
          "en": "\"Please enter a valid email address,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 89,
          "start": 269.4,
          "end": 270.843,
          "en": "or something like this.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 90,
          "start": 272.28,
          "end": 273.93,
          "en": "So that's the first check.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 91,
          "start": 273.93,
          "end": 278.93,
          "en": "The next check is to check if the password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 92,
          "start": 279.78,
          "end": 283.5,
          "en": "after trimming it to remove excess wide space",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 93,
          "start": 283.5,
          "end": 285.42,
          "en": "at the beginning or end,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 94,
          "start": 285.42,
          "end": 287.13,
          "en": "if it then has a length",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 95,
          "start": 287.13,
          "end": 290.073,
          "en": "that's smaller than eight, let's say,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 96,
          "start": 291.06,
          "end": 294.72,
          "en": "so that we force the user to pick a password",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 97,
          "start": 294.72,
          "end": 299.72,
          "en": "that's at least eight characters long for security reasons.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 98,
          "start": 300.316,
          "end": 302.452,
          "en": "So if we have a shorter password,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 99,
          "start": 302.452,
          "end": 306.892,
          "en": "I'll add a password field to the errors object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 100,
          "start": 306.892,
          "end": 310.191,
          "en": "And in there, we could have an error message like,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 101,
          "start": 310.191,
          "end": 314.64,
          "en": "\"Password must be at least 8 characters long,\"",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 102,
          "start": 314.64,
          "end": 316.623,
          "en": "to tell the user what's wrong.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 103,
          "start": 318.36,
          "end": 321.96,
          "en": "Though of course, just by creating this errors object,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 104,
          "start": 321.96,
          "end": 324.003,
          "en": "we won't do anything.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 105,
          "start": 324.87,
          "end": 329.82,
          "en": "Instead, we of course, need to kind of pass this object here",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 106,
          "start": 329.82,
          "end": 334.82,
          "en": "to our front end to our form and output it there.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 107,
          "start": 334.83,
          "end": 338.32,
          "en": "And you did learn in this course how that can be achieved",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 108,
          "start": 339.24,
          "end": 342.183,
          "en": "with help of the use form state hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 109,
          "start": 343.11,
          "end": 346.53,
          "en": "So, here in the auth-form.js file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 110,
          "start": 346.53,
          "end": 351.53,
          "en": "we can actually import something from react-dom",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 111,
          "start": 352.08,
          "end": 355.83,
          "en": "and that something is the use form state hook,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 112,
          "start": 355.83,
          "end": 358.773,
          "en": "about which you learned earlier in the course already.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 113,
          "start": 360.12,
          "end": 362.88,
          "en": "There, you also learned that this hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 114,
          "start": 362.88,
          "end": 365.49,
          "en": "only works in a client component,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 115,
          "start": 365.49,
          "end": 369.03,
          "en": "and therefore I'll add the 'use client' directive here,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 116,
          "start": 369.03,
          "end": 372.033,
          "en": "at the top of the auth-form.js file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 117,
          "start": 373.62,
          "end": 374.91,
          "en": "Well, and then with that,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 118,
          "start": 374.91,
          "end": 379.32,
          "en": "we can call use form state here in the auth form.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 119,
          "start": 379.32,
          "end": 383.79,
          "en": "And we now need to pass the Server Action",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 120,
          "start": 383.79,
          "end": 387.69,
          "en": "that should be handled with help of the use form state hook",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 121,
          "start": 387.69,
          "end": 390.48,
          "en": "as a first argument to that hook.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 122,
          "start": 390.48,
          "end": 393.15,
          "en": "And that Server Action, of course,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 123,
          "start": 393.15,
          "end": 396.483,
          "en": "is that signup action I'm working on here.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 124,
          "start": 397.47,
          "end": 400.8,
          "en": "Therefore, we should actually export this function",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 125,
          "start": 400.8,
          "end": 402.993,
          "en": "from the auth actions file,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 126,
          "start": 404.1,
          "end": 407.25,
          "en": "so that in auth-form.js we can import it,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 127,
          "start": 407.25,
          "end": 411.65999999999997,
          "en": "and import this signup function from the actions folder",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 128,
          "start": 411.65999999999997,
          "end": 414.27,
          "en": "and the auth actions file.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 129,
          "start": 414.27,
          "end": 417.75,
          "en": "And it's then this signup action that will be passed",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 130,
          "start": 417.75,
          "end": 420.483,
          "en": "as a first argument to use form state.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 131,
          "start": 421.77,
          "end": 425.01,
          "en": "The second argument as you learned is the initial state,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 132,
          "start": 425.01,
          "end": 428.28,
          "en": "and in my case here, that will be an empty object.",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 133,
          "start": 428.28,
          "end": 432.15,
          "en": "And then we'll get back an array with exactly two elements,",
          "zh": ""
        },
        {
          "id": 134,
          "start": 432.15,
          "end": 435.66,
          "en": "where the first element will be the form state,",
